<BaseLayout title="Shadow Copy inventory" description="How Nova Corp retains earlier versions, tests recovery and records 30 shadow-copy objects." breadcrumbs={[{label:"NOVA-FILES01",href:"systems/nova-files01/"},{label:"Shadow Copies"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">File server / Previous Versions</div><h1>Shadow Copies</h1><p class="lead">An earlier saved version of a file can help an employee recover from a mistaken edit or deletion without restoring the whole server.</p></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container grid-main"><article class="prose">
<h2>What are these objects?</h2><p>Windows Volume Shadow Copy Service records point-in-time versions. The public inventory contains 30 VSS objects across two volume identifiers. Nine of the ten recorded data-volume objects are marked client-accessible; the remaining records are not. Not every VSS object is an employee-accessible Previous Version.</p>
<h2>Why keep earlier versions?</h2><p><strong>Problem:</strong> Moyo accidentally changes or deletes a file on the IT drive. Recreating the file wastes time and a full-server restore is unnecessary.</p><p><strong>Solution:</strong> Use Previous Versions to open a suitable recovery point, inspect the file and copy only the required version back. Nova Corp's D: Shadow Copies are scheduled at 07:00 and 12:00.</p>
<OriginalPdfEvidenceGallery ids={["shadow-copy-two-triggers","shadow-copy-created","shadow-copy-storage"]} heading="Actual schedule and snapshot storage"/>
<h2>How the recovery was tested</h2><ol><li>Create a disposable test file through the employee-facing Z: drive and create a snapshot.</li><li>Modify the live file, capture the modified version in a later snapshot, then delete the live file.</li><li>Open Z: Properties → Previous Versions, select a recovery point and inspect the historical file.</li><li>Copy only the file back and recheck its contents.</li></ol>
<pre><code>{'Test-Path "Z:\\CR010-Shadow-Recovery-Test.txt"\nGet-Content "Z:\\CR010-Shadow-Recovery-Test.txt"'}</code></pre><p><strong>Expected:</strong> False after deletion; True and the selected historical version's contents after copying it back.</p><p><strong>Actual:</strong> The journal records False before recovery and True with the captured modified version after recovery. A one-hour difference between server and client display times was traced to timezone presentation, not missing recovery data.</p>
<OriginalPdfEvidenceGallery ids={["shadow-copy-previous-it","shadow-copy-deleted-file"]} heading="Actual Previous Versions recovery"/>
<p>A later separate CR-015 exercise proved an earlier file version matched the original SHA-256 exactly while the modified live file had a different hash. <a href={base+"reference/explore/files/SHADOW_COPY_RECOVERY/"}>Read the full recorded comparison and test details →</a></p>
<h2>Inspect the 30 recorded objects</h2><EngineeringSourceEmbed sourcePath="docs/explore/files/VSS.md" title="Original VSS inventory and limits"/>
<h2>Recovery limits and related tests</h2><p>These objects are not 30 independently tested restores. Storage is shared with the underlying lab; Previous Versions are not an independent off-site backup.</p><p><a href={base+"files/backup/"}>Separate Windows Server Backup →</a> · <a href={base+"incidents/backup-target-unavailable/"}>Controlled backup target failure →</a></p>
